╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ grouped_crz_brickwork                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz block is extremely parameter-efficient (only 4 shared rotation         │
│                          │ parameters per block), which yields low train-test gap but caps expressivity. To improve  │
│                          │ accuracy without exploding parameter count, this rewrite increases parameter diversity in │
│                          │ a structured way:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Replace fully collective rotations with **grouped** single-qubit rotations (4 groups →  │
│                          │ shared parameters within each group).                                                     │
│                          │ - Keep the entangling structure **fixed** using a cube/brickwork-like CZ pattern for      │
│                          │ efficient mixing.                                                                         │
│                          │ - Add a small number of **parametrized entanglers** using CRZ on disjoint edges (to make  │
│                          │ pairwise correlations trainable while limiting parameters).                               │
│                          │ - Use a final grouped RZ to add phase fine-tuning before measurement.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targets better validation/test accuracy and lower L2 by giving the optimizer         │
│                          │ additional controlled degrees of freedom, while maintaining moderate parameter efficiency │
│                          │ (far below the large-parameter seed baselines).                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
